<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 382.4 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 382.4 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of February 6 raised 382.4 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 535.9 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 96.28 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    13.96 (14.08)	  48.3   (55.2)</p>
<p>    Six months		14.98 (15.56)	  86.6  (135.5)</p>
<p>    12 months		 15.37 (15.84)	 116.3  (145.1)</p>
<p>    24 months		 16.34 (17.14)	 131.2  (200.1)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at $1,549.25 to the U.S dollar on Tuesday from $1,549.75 at the beginning of last week and 1,590 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
